+# Mission 10 Progress — Automated CI Bring-Up
+
+## 2026-11-26 checkpoint
+
+- Remote overlay branch was verified at `d0379403aa094e6808fa581dc91dc2b10fe8cd98` before this change; its materialized tree was `b51f7ec073bc8278dcf5b879a0ad772a4c20fdc6`.
+- Workflow run `45864893829`: Linux host job passed. macOS `ios-arm64` reached generated MSL validation but failed because `SDL2/SDL.h` was not on the compiler include path through `data/dynos.h`; IPA packaging was skipped. The root cause was not a game-renderer error.
+- Patch 29 obtains SDL2 compiler flags using `pkg-config --cflags sdl2`. It preserves patch 28's Lua include path. Exact replay of patches 1–29 yields tree `f9722948b63a5263014a0d2eba973fc6240baf13`.
+- On that exact materialized source, `make -j2` passed. Four focused tests passed normally and under ASan/UBSan (sandbox leak detection disabled): `run_gfx_metal_coopdx_shader_test.sh`, `run_gfx_sdl_metal_layer_test.sh`, `run_gfx_texture_cache_rewind_test.sh`, and `run_touchscreen_controls_math_test.sh`.
+- Workflow change: the macOS iPhoneOS job is independent of the Linux host job; both jobs remain present and continue to report their own status.
+- Not yet verified: publishing this checkpoint, a subsequent Apple runner start, iPhoneOS app compilation/linking, IPA creation, archive validation, or physical-device behavior.
+
+## Next steps
+
+1. Update the overlay patch/checksum series and expected materialized tree for this documentation checkpoint.
+2. Validate clean patch replay, shell/YAML syntax, Linux build/tests.
+3. Publish without force and verify branch HEAD.
+4. Attempt one manual `ios-metal.yml` dispatch; if the current session cannot reach GitHub, preserve the commit and report that exact external blocker rather than claiming a run.
+5. On successful Apple run, inspect full logs and IPA evidence before reporting build success.
